# Activity scene — the coworker, second time: a colleague's birthday.
# cast.md § 5.1: invitations to a colleague's birthday; dialogue-context.md
# § 10 the studied non-celebration of birthdays.
# TODO: authenticity check

It's someone's birthday, you realize, as the cake comes out of the back of the restaurant with the candles already lit.
Everyone starts singing.
- Step outside.
	[signal arg="CONVICTION:1"]
	You step out into the parking lot until it's over. After a minute {GameState.coworker_name} comes out too.
	"Oh — right. Birthdays. Sorry. I totally forgot." They don't make it weird. "Want me to bring you a piece? It's not a birthday piece. It's just cake."
- Stay, and don't sing.
	[signal arg="EXPOSE:1"]
	You stay, and you don't sing, and you clap at the end with everyone else. The candles go out. Nothing happens. It's a cake.
